LPDDR5 Controller IP Summary

The lpddr5c IP is an open-source LPDDR5/LPDDR5X Memory Controller designed for ASIC and FPGA implementations. The controller targets JEDEC JESD209-5 compliant LPDDR5/LPDDR5X memories and provides a complete digital controller architecture interfacing with the DRAM PHY through a DFI 5.0 compliant interface. The controller supports dual-channel operation, x16 data width per channel, and is designed to achieve data rates up to 6400 MT/s (LPDDR5) and 8533 MT/s (LPDDR5X).
The architecture consists of a Command Scheduler, Data Path, Register Configuration (APB4), Refresh Controller, Training Controller, Low Power Management, and a DFI Interface Adapter. The controller implements the complete LPDDR5 initialization flow, training algorithms, refresh scheduling, ECC support, low-power management, and timing parameter configuration.
The current project status indicates that all eight core RTL modules have been completed, including the top-level integration, command scheduler, data path, register configuration, refresh controller, training controller, low-power manager, and DFI interface. The remaining work is focused on verification infrastructure, including the testbench, simulation environment, and performance optimization.

